HERE IS SOME CODE THAT SAVES REBOUND SIMULATION DATA TO DISK, AND THEN
RELOADS IT TO PRODUCE A MOVIE. HERE ARE THE STEPS

1. python rebound_example_vis.py

THIS SAVE DATA TO DISK AT REGULAR INTERVALS OF THE SIMULATION.
SIMULATION ARCHIVES ARE VERY CONVENIENT BUT TAKE UP A LOT OF SPACE ON DISK.
WE MAY WANT TO TRY ALTERNATIVE WAYS OF SAVING DATA IN THE FUTURE.

2. python simulation_movie_pts.py .

THIS PRODUCE PNG SNAPSHOTS SHOWING THE PARTICLE POSITIONS:tmp_movie_000.png, tmp_movie_001.png,etc...

